Package: tumr
Title: A collection of tools for visualizing and analyzing longitudinal tumor growth data
Version: 0.7.2
Authors@R: c(
  person("Tian", "Zhao", role='aut', email="gapomochi@gmail.com", comment=c(ORCID="0009-0006-9527-286X")),
  person("Sydney", "Plowman", role='aut'),
  person("Patrick", "Breheny", role=c("aut","cre"),email="patrick-breheny@uiowa.edu", comment=c(ORCID="0000-0002-0650-1119"))
  )
Description: This package provides tools for analyzing longitudinal tumor
    growth data, including visualization of growth trajectories, model fits,
    and diagnostics. Statistical methods include linear mixed-effects,
    nonlinear, and Bayesian models, along with tumor doubling time
    estimation, response feature analysis, simulation, and power and
    sample size calculations.
Depends: R (>= 4.3.0)
